{"repositoryId":418128371,"availability":"available","full":"jhrcook/coffee-counter-appwrite-demo","name":"coffee-counter-appwrite-demo","description":"A demonstration of using an Appwrite backend for a Coffee Counting app.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":6,"forks":0,"created":"2021-10-17T12:44:00Z","updated":"2021-10-17T19:06:29Z","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["appwrite","demo","fastapi","pydantic","python"],"demo":"https://www.python.org/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T13:33:24.726Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T13:33:24.726Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T13:33:24.726Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T13:33:24.726Z","stars":6,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This repo serves as a demonstration of using Appwrite's Database services in a Python application. The demo would be part of an app that tracks coffee consumption. The API is written with FastAPI with data validation by pydantic.","My current working version of this app (not using Appwrite, at the moment) can be found here.","The overall point of this app is to serve as a method for tracking my coffee consumption. I want more than just the number of cups, but also the coffee bag that was used and the lifetime of the coffee bags. You can read more about the purpose and the various tools I have built around the API on my website."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jhrcook/coffee-counter-appwrite-demo/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"b5d6e54fb8bfef74e7592fece2d272c94b210cc73d2466c667f26c2c5dedad9c","extractedAt":"2026-10-18T13:33:24.836Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T13:33:24.836Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This repo serves as a demonstration of using Appwrite's Database services in a Python application. The demo would be part of an app that tracks coffee consumption. The API is written with FastAPI with data validation by pydantic.","sourc